# Commands run by the launchd job com.redwood.demo (see com.redwood.demo.plist).
# Reading the APFS volume the kernel mounted on /private/var/apfs-check (boot-arg
# apfs_check=3), from user space.  The three roads, over one fixed set of files
# (/usr/sbin: 32 files, 47.8 MB) so that two kernels can be compared on equal terms:
#   mapping          the only road that makes the driver's vnop_pagein run
#   small read(2)s   what the compressed path is worst at
#   large read(2)s   the control: a piece per decompression even before any caching
/redwood/bin/apfs_mmap_test mmap /private/var/apfs-check/usr/sbin
/redwood/bin/apfs_mmap_test read /private/var/apfs-check/usr/sbin 4096
/redwood/bin/apfs_mmap_test read /private/var/apfs-check/usr/sbin 65536
